# UI Component Conventions

Follow these patterns when creating or editing components in `src/components/ui/` (shadcn-style primitives).

## Imports

- Use namespace import for React: `import * as React from "react"`.
- Put a blank line between React/external imports and internal imports.
- Use path alias for utilities: `import { cn } from "@/lib/utils/cn"`.
- Use double quotes for import specifiers.

```tsx
import * as React from "react"
import { Slot } from "@radix-ui/react-slot"
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority"

import { cn } from "@/lib/utils/cn"
```

## Component Definition

- Use **named function declarations** (not arrow functions).
- Destructure props with `className` first, then variant/size/options, then `...props`.
- Type props as `React.ComponentProps<"element">` for the root DOM element; extend with `VariantProps<typeof variants>` and optional props (e.g. `asChild?: boolean`) when needed.

```tsx
function Button({
  className,
  variant = "default",
  size = "default",
  asChild = false,
  ...props
}: React.ComponentProps<"button"> &
  VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> & {
    asChild?: boolean
  }) {
  // ...
}
```

## Styling

- Use **class-variance-authority (cva)** for components with multiple variants/sizes; define `baseClasses` and a `variants` object with `defaultVariants`.
- Use **Tailwind** with theme tokens (e.g. `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `hover:bg-primary/90`, `border`, `bg-destructive`). Support **dark mode** with `dark:` where relevant.
- Include **accessibility** in base classes: `focus-visible:`, `aria-invalid:`, `disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50`, and consistent focus rings (e.g. `focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px]`).
- Merge classes with **cn()**: when using cva, pass `className` into the variants call so cva merges it, e.g. `className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}`. When not using cva, use `className={cn("base-classes", className)}` so callers can override or extend.

## Data Attributes

- Set **data-slot** on the root element with the component name in kebab-case (e.g. `data-slot="button"`, `data-slot="card-header"`). Optionally set **data-variant** and **data-size** (or similar) when the component has variants for styling or debugging.

```tsx
<Comp
  data-slot="button"
  data-variant={variant}
  data-size={size}
  className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}
  {...props}
/>
```

## Polymorphic / asChild

- When the component can render as a different element or child (e.g. “asChild”), use **@radix-ui/react-slot**: resolve `Comp = asChild ? Slot : "button"` and render `<Comp ... />` so a single child can replace the root.

## Exports

- **Named exports** only. Export the component and, if using cva, the **variants** object (e.g. `buttonVariants`) so other components can reuse variant styles.

```tsx
export { Button, buttonVariants }
```

## Formatting

- Indent with 2 spaces.
- Use trailing commas in multi-line objects (variants, defaultVariants, props).
- Keep base class strings in cva readable; break long lines only when necessary.
